om/FavioVazquez/ds-cheatsheets\"><code>FavioVazquez/ds-cheatsheets</code></a></li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-31T08:38:46.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Supplement: Cheat Sheets</h2>","itemHTML":"<li>Statistics\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/wzchen/probability_cheatsheet\"><code>wzchen/probability-cheatsheet</code></a> - \"This cheatsheet is a 10-page reference in probability that covers a semester's worth of introductory probability. The cheatsheet is based off of Harvard's introductory probability course, Stat 110. It is co-authored by former Stat 110 Teaching Fellow William Chen and Stat 110 Professor Joe Blitzstein.\"</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://stanford.edu/~shervine/teaching/cs-229/refresher-probabilities-statistics\">Probabilities and statistics refresher</a> cheat sheet from <a href=\"https://github.com/afshinea/stanford-cs-229-machine-learning\">Stanford CS 229</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/afshinea/stanford-cs-229-machine-learning\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">12.9k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":12858,\"repo\":\"afshinea/stanford-cs-229-machine-learning\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--></li>\n</ul>\n</li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-31T08:38:46.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"rust-unofficial/awesome-rust","categoryHTML":"<h2>Libraries</h2><h4>Machine learning</h4>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/smartcorelib/smartcore\">smartcorelib/smartcore</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/smartcorelib/smartcore\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">200</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":200,\"repo\":\"smartcorelib/smartcore\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> — Machine Learning Library In Rust <a href=\"https://smartcorelib.org/\"><img src=\"https://img.shields.io/circleci/build/github/smartcorelib/smartcore\" alt=\"Build Status\"></a></li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-31T05:41:21.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"hangtwenty/dive-into-machine-learning","categoryHTML":"<h2>Supplement: Learning Pandas well</h2>","itemHTML":"<li>Bookmarks for scaling <code>pandas</code> and alternatives\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://dask.org/\"><code>dask</code></a>: A Pandas-like interface, but for larger-than-memory data and \"under the hood\" parallelism.</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://vaex.io\"><code>vaex</code></a>\n<ul>\n<li>\"Out-of-Core hybrid Apache Arrow/NumPy DataFrame for Python, ML, visualize and explore big tabular data at a billion rows per second\"</li>\n<li>\"It calculates statistics such as mean, sum, count, standard deviation etc, on an N-dimensional grid for more than a billion (10^9) samples/rows per second. Visualization is done using histograms, density plots and 3d volume rendering, allowing interactive exploration of big data. Vaex uses memory mapping, zero memory copy policy and lazy computations for best performance (no memory wasted).\"</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>See also: the MLOps section <a href=\"#production-deployment-mlops\">later in this guid